  "body": "Add a guide page on units and coordinates. Several real bugs and reviews came from confusion here (for example, a schema telling an agent the wrong unit, which would have placed a holder 25.4 times off), so users need it too.\n\nCover:\n- **Document units:** what the project's unit is, what the posted program's unit is, and how they relate (inch and mm programs).\n- **Imported models:** how STEP declares its unit and how CamCraft reads it (an inch STEP is scaled to mm on import); STL and OBJ have no unit, so how they're read; the 25.4x check against a known dimension.\n- **Tools and tool libraries:** which unit a library file's numbers are in (`units` in the `camcraft-tools` envelope).\n- **Coordinates:** the model frame, the setup's WCS (origin and axes, how picks set it), the work offset (G54..., how a setup chooses it) and the machine frame; where Z zero sits and why it matters.\n- **Stock:** how it's placed relative to the model and the WCS.\n- **Rotary and lathe:** what A/B/C and the lathe's X (diameter or radius) mean in CamCraft's programs.\n\nDiagrams would help here (a part with its WCS triad and the machine zero).\n\nDone means: a units and coordinates page in the guide covering document, import, tool-library and program units, and the model/WCS/work-offset/machine frames, linked from setups.md and the migration page (#1240).\n",
